From ac5d1771463cbb39dcec58cb7a6288a6f03a562b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:44:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add tag pictures: ^I<name>^ shows a .png or .tga from
 uifiles/zeal/tagicons

Guilds keep asking for their own logos as tag markers. Building each one
into Zeal means a code change and a release per guild, and a painted logo
can't be drawn as an extruded shape anyway. Tag pictures work like the
target ring textures instead: drop a file in a folder and use it.

- uifiles/zeal/tagicons/<name>.png or .tga, where <name> is 1 to 6 letters
  or digits in any case. ^I<name>^ draws that picture flat, facing the
  camera the way the nameplate text does, sitting where the shape would.
  A picture takes over from a built-in guild icon with the same code
  (EUR.png replaces the built-in EUR icon for whoever has the file).
- Only players with the file see the picture. Others see the guild's
  built-in shape, or just the text for a code that isn't a guild. If
  the file won't load, the tag falls back to the built-in shape, or a
  white arrow when there is none.
- Files are checked before they are decoded: the PNG or true-color TGA
  header must give a size of at most 512 pixels a side, and the file must
  be at most 1 MB. Anything else is skipped with a chat message, once.
- Each picture is loaded once (a managed texture) and released with the
  other tag resources; /tag icons lists the pictures, reads the folder
  again and reloads changed files.
- The tag chat line reads "(Picture EUR)" for a picture tag.
- README: document tag pictures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
